# Analyser diagnostics through the tcl-lsp MCP server (cached build; may lag HEAD afe2f2d8 slightly), dialect tcl9.0 unless noted.
# Format: fixture: [CODE Lline message]. "FALSE" marks a diagnostic contradicted by every tclsh that runs the fixture; "MISSED" marks a fault tclsh reports that the analyser does not.
e01-catch-codes.tcl: none
e02-catch-options.tcl: none
e03-return-code-break-from-proc.tcl: none
e04-bare-break-in-proc.tcl: [W302 L9 catch without result var]; MISSED: bare break/continue leaving procs b and c (tclsh: invoked "break" outside of a loop, always)
e05-try-on-trap.tcl: none
e06-try-finally-overrides.tcl: none
e07-throw.tcl: [E002 L4 Too few arguments for 'throw'] (true; inside catch)
e08-error-info-code.tcl: [W210 L10 Variable 'nosuch' is read before it is set] (true; deliberate failing read inside catch)
e09-errorstack.tcl: none
e10-errorline.tcl: none
e11-custom-codes.tcl: none
e12-break-through-eval-uplevel.tcl: [W302 L10]; MISSED: proc ub's uplevel 1 {break} always errors
e13-return-options.tcl: none (return notreached after return -level 2 callee not flagged; no false positive)
e14-dead-after-control.tcl: [I230 L6 Condition '1' is always true] [W302 L7] [W302 L8 x2]; MISSED: no diagnostic for unreachable commands after return, error, break, throw, if/else-both-return (the optimiser does find them: O107)
e15-catch-defines-vars.tcl: [W302 L2]; no W210 after catch body or catch result/options vars (backlog entry not reproduced on this build)
e16-errorinfo-accumulation.tcl: none
e17-loop-body-codes.tcl: [W242 L9 for termination cannot be proven] FALSE-ish (step is break) [W210 L9 Variable 'z' is read before it is set] FALSE
e18-try-in-proc-return.tcl: none
e19-native-errorcodes.tcl: none
e20-toplevel-return-source.tcl: none
e21-handler-options.tcl: none
e22-uncaught-toplevel-break.tcl: none; MISSED: top-level break in a script file always errors
e23-uncaught-toplevel-custom.tcl: none
e24-uncaught-error-trace.tcl: none
e25-catch-for-loop-var.tcl: [W210 L2 Variable 'i' is read before it is set] FALSE (span = whole catch command) [W302 L4] [W210 L4 Variable 'j' is read before it is set] FALSE [W242 L4] FALSE-ish; proc b ([catch …] inside if) gets no W210
e26-for-break-step.tcl: [W242 L2 for termination cannot be proven: 'i' never modified by the step or body] FALSE-ish (the step is break)
e27-optimiser-try-finally.tcl: none
e28-optimiser-return-level0.tcl: none
e29-finally-reads-body-var.tcl: [W220 L2 Assignment to 'a' is never read] FALSE (the finally clause reads it)
e30-after-return-level0.tcl: [W210 L2 Variable 'y' is read before it is set] FALSE (return -level 0 does not leave the procedure)

# Discriminating variants (not fixture files), tcl9.0:
# proc a {} { catch {for {set i 0} {$i < 3} {incr i} {}} r ; return $r }          -> W210 'i' FALSE
# proc b {} { catch { for {set i 0} {$i < 3} {incr i} {}} r ; return $r }         -> W210 'i' FALSE
# proc c {} { catch {set x 1; for {set i 0} {$i < 3} {incr i} {}} r ; return $r }  -> W210 'i' FALSE
# proc d {} { catch {foreach i {1 2} {puts $i}} r ; return $r }                    -> none
# proc e {} { catch {while {[set q 1]} {break}} r ; return $r }                    -> none
# proc b {} { try { for {set j 0} {$j < 3} {incr j} { puts $j } } on error {m} { return $m } ; return ok }  -> none
# proc e {} { eval { for {set e 0} {$e < 2} {incr e} {} } ; return ok }           -> none
# for {...} {...} {break} {...} without catch, in a proc                             -> W242 only
# proc t {} { try { set a 1; return 1 } finally { puts $a } }                         -> W220 'a' FALSE
# proc w {} { catch {error x} ; return $nn }                                        -> W210 'nn' (true)

# Release gating, tcl8.4: try, throw, info errorstack, namespace unknown -> W002; return -level -> W004; catch {…} r o -> nothing (MISSED: 8.4 catch takes one variable, tclsh 8.4 fails 'wrong # args').
# tcl8.5: try, throw, lmap -> W002 and also W123 'Unknown command' (double report; 8.4 gives W002 only).

# Optimiser (MCP optimize):
# e27, profile full/aggressive, tcl8.6 and tcl9.0: O107 "Eliminate unreachable dead code" deletes `puts fin` from `try { return 1 } finally { puts fin }`; aggressive also O103 folds [t] to 1. WRONG: tclsh prints "fin" then "1"; rewritten script prints "1".
# e28, profile full, tcl8.6: O107 deletes `puts reached-v` after `return -level 0 lvl0`. WRONG: tclsh prints "reached-v" then ""; rewritten prints "lvl0".
# try { error x } on error {m} { return h } finally { puts fin }: O107 deletes `puts fin`. WRONG.
# Profile readability (the LSP default): no rewrites.
# Correct O107: code after return, error, throw, return -code error, return -code ok (level 1), continue in foreach; return -code break/continue procs are not inlined.
